{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_bdrk_spdkbo3rpskbcbg5fvmelbdl2rthoitgm4ageapom25yaxclw4qa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01HyMhapUvvzgtgxx1p6bogT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/harvest-translate-shxmUI/translated_rust/.contracts/SHARED_RULES.md","content":"# Shared translation rules (libsodium 1.0.23 -> Rust cdylib)\n\nYou are translating part of libsodium into a single Rust cdylib. The C source is\nin `c_src/libsodium/`. DO NOT modify anything in `c_src/`. Reference C behavior EXACTLY;\ndo not fix bugs. Produce byte-identical output for identical inputs.\n\n## Build environment facts (CRITICAL)\nThe CMake build defines NO `HAVE_*`, NO `CONFIGURED`, NO `NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN`,\nNO `__SSE2__` etc. So:\n- Only the PORTABLE / `ref` code paths compile. SIMD `#ifdef HAVE_*` blocks are\n  DEAD (skip those files/branches). Translate ONLY the reference implementation.\n- Endianness helpers use the byte-by-byte (non-memcpy) path. Target is x86-64 LE,\n  but always translate the generic LE load/store logic from common.h.\n- `SODIUM_C99(.field =)` designated initializers are just struct field inits.\n\n## Namespace / linker symbol names (CRITICAL for the ABI)\n`c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/private/quirks.h` renames many internal source-level\nnames, e.g. `#define blake2b _sodium_blake2b`. The EXPORTED linker symbol is the\nright-hand side. Your `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` name MUST equal the FINAL linker symbol.\n- Public API functions like `crypto_hash_sha256` export under their own name.\n- Internal helpers renamed by quirks.h export with the `_sodium_` prefix.\nYour assigned symbol-list file lists the EXACT linker names you must export. Match them.\n\n## Rust conventions for this crate\n- Every exported symbol: `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn NAME(...) -> ... {}`\n  with C ABI types from `core::ffi` (`c_int`, `c_char`, etc.). Use `unsafe extern \"C\"`\n  when the body dereferences raw pointers.\n- Exported data symbols (implementation structs, tables) use\n  `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub static NAME: T = ...;` matching the C object's layout.\n- Preserve exact order of validation / error checks and exact return values.\n- Signatures: C `unsigned long long` -> `u64`; `size_t` -> `usize`; `int` -> `c_int`;\n  `unsigned char *` -> `*mut u8` / `*const u8`; `void *` -> `*mut c_void`.\n- Internal (non-exported) helpers can be safe Rust; keep arithmetic wrapping where C\n  relies on unsigned wraparound (use `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_mul`).\n  Rust `--release` still traps on overflow in debug arithmetic checks if `overflow-checks`\n  is on; this crate builds release (checks off) but be safe and use wrapping ops in\n  crypto core loops.\n\n## Cross-module calls\nThis is ONE cdylib. To call a function implemented in another module (e.g. you need\n`crypto_stream_chacha20` but it's in another package), declare it in an\n`extern \"C\" { fn crypto_stream_chacha20(...); }` block using its FINAL linker name and\nthe correct C signature (read the header in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`). The\nlinker resolves it within the same .so. Do NOT re-implement functions owned by another\npackage. Foundation functions already implemented and callable this way include:\n`sodium_misuse`, `sodium_memzero`, `randombytes_buf`, `sodium_memcmp`,\n`crypto_verify_16/32/64`, plus all `sodium_runtime_has_*`.\n\n## Constants\nRead the public headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/` for the exact numeric\nvalues of every `_BYTES`, `_KEYBYTES`, etc. and the `..._bytes()`-style accessor\nfunctions (which just `return X_BYTES;`).\n\n## Your deliverable\nWrite Rust `.rs` files ONLY inside your assigned module directory (e.g. `src/primitives/`).\nWire them via your module's `mod.rs` (declare submodules `pub mod foo;`). Do not edit\n`src/lib.rs` or other packages' directories. When done, the crate must still compile:\nrun `cargo build --release` from the crate root and fix errors in YOUR files.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":168536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":301,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8da51a24-6452-4245-bede-fa7b9c735887","uuid":"2927b358-63bb-42e5-9650-628c6aa87cf4","timestamp":"2026-08-05T01:58:57.911Z"}
