{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014B5SxYZWPMfMTMBiStBANd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Shared translation rules (libsodium 1.0.23 -> Rust cdylib)\n2\t\n3\tYou are translating part of libsodium into a single Rust cdylib. The C source is\n4\tin `c_src/libsodium/`. DO NOT modify anything in `c_src/`. Reference C behavior EXACTLY;\n5\tdo not fix bugs. Produce byte-identical output for identical inputs.\n6\t\n7\t## Build environment facts (CRITICAL)\n8\tThe CMake build defines NO `HAVE_*`, NO `CONFIGURED`, NO `NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN`,\n9\tNO `__SSE2__` etc. So:\n10\t- Only the PORTABLE / `ref` code paths compile. SIMD `#ifdef HAVE_*` blocks are\n11\t  DEAD (skip those files/branches). Translate ONLY the reference implementation.\n12\t- Endianness helpers use the byte-by-byte (non-memcpy) path. Target is x86-64 LE,\n13\t  but always translate the generic LE load/store logic from common.h.\n14\t- `SODIUM_C99(.field =)` designated initializers are just struct field inits.\n15\t\n16\t## Namespace / linker symbol names (CRITICAL for the ABI)\n17\t`c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/private/quirks.h` renames many internal source-level\n18\tnames, e.g. `#define blake2b _sodium_blake2b`. The EXPORTED linker symbol is the\n19\tright-hand side. Your `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` name MUST equal the FINAL linker symbol.\n20\t- Public API functions like `crypto_hash_sha256` export under their own name.\n21\t- Internal helpers renamed by quirks.h export with the `_sodium_` prefix.\n22\tYour assigned symbol-list file lists the EXACT linker names you must export. Match them.\n23\t\n24\t## Rust conventions for this crate\n25\t- Every exported symbol: `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn NAME(...) -> ... {}`\n26\t  with C ABI types from `core::ffi` (`c_int`, `c_char`, etc.). Use `unsafe extern \"C\"`\n27\t  when the body dereferences raw pointers.\n28\t- Exported data symbols (implementation structs, tables) use\n29\t  `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub static NAME: T = ...;` matching the C object's layout.\n30\t- Preserve exact order of validation / error checks and exact return values.\n31\t- Signatures: C `unsigned long long` -> `u64`; `size_t` -> `usize`; `int` -> `c_int`;\n32\t  `unsigned char *` -> `*mut u8` / `*const u8`; `void *` -> `*mut c_void`.\n33\t- Internal (non-exported) helpers can be safe Rust; keep arithmetic wrapping where C\n34\t  relies on unsigned wraparound (use `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_mul`).\n35\t  Rust `--release` still traps on overflow in debug arithmetic checks if `overflow-checks`\n36\t  is on; this crate builds release (checks off) but be safe and use wrapping ops in\n37\t  crypto core loops.\n38\t\n39\t## Cross-module calls\n40\tThis is ONE cdylib. To call a function implemented in another module (e.g. you need\n41\t`crypto_stream_chacha20` but it's in another package), declare it in an\n42\t`extern \"C\" { fn crypto_stream_chacha20(...); }` block using its FINAL linker name and\n43\tthe correct C signature (read the header in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`). The\n44\tlinker resolves it within the same .so. Do NOT re-implement functions owned by another\n45\tpackage. Foundation functions already implemented and callable this way include:\n46\t`sodium_misuse`, `sodium_memzero`, `randombytes_buf`, `sodium_memcmp`,\n47\t`crypto_verify_16/32/64`, plus all `sodium_runtime_has_*`.\n48\t\n49\t## Constants\n50\tRead the public headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/` for the exact numeric\n51\tvalues of every `_BYTES`, `_KEYBYTES`, etc. and the `..._bytes()`-style accessor\n52\tfunctions (which just `return X_BYTES;`).\n53\t\n54\t## Your deliverable\n55\tWrite Rust `.rs` files ONLY inside your assigned module directory (e.g. `src/primitives/`).\n56\tWire them via your module's `mod.rs` (declare submodules `pub mod foo;`). Do not edit\n57\t`src/lib.rs` or other packages' directories. When done, the crate must still compile:\n58\trun `cargo build --release` from the crate root and fix errors in YOUR files.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01H7ntT1vT3KzfNR94ibyhCd","session_id":"8da51a24-6452-4245-bede-fa7b9c735887","uuid":"0167bae9-81f9-4af2-ac6f-e1704973f2ab","timestamp":"2026-08-05T02:41:28.544Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate P3 aead"}
