ges: `crypto_core_hchacha20`, `crypto_stream_salsa20_xor`, `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_ext[_xor_ic]`, `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_xor`, `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_init/update/final`, and `sodium_memzero`. I did NOT redefine these (would cause duplicate-symbol link errors); I only call them via extern. The genuinely-unclaimed ones I implemented: `crypto_core_hsalsa20`, `crypto_generichash_init/update/final`.\n- Reproduced C bugs/quirks exactly: e.g. secretstream's `(0x10 - (sizeof block) + mlen) & 0xf` padding (operator-precedence bug), the `(-(h == correct))` self-compare idiom in hmac verify, the xchacha ietf_ext single-pass oversized-message path, and validation/return-value ordering.\n- The one undefined symbol in the .so is `_sodium_softaes_block_encrypt` (P5), which resolves at link within the same cdylib — expected.\n- The aegis `implementation` struct layout matches C (two fn pointers, encrypt_detached then decrypt_detached), exported as `pub static` data symbols; `pick_best` sets the static pointer to soft impl and returns 0.","usage":{"total_tokens":241632,"tool_uses":71,"duration_ms":914430},"uuid":"588047b0-d8f9-4d96-890c-51873f4a9f49","session_id":"8da51a24-6452-4245-bede-fa7b9c735887"}
