se`, and — importantly — `sodium_base642bin`/`sodium_bin2base64`. The latter two are listed in P4 but are **already defined by the foundation `src/codecs.rs`**, so I call them via `extern \"C\"` rather than redefining (a redefinition would cause duplicate-symbol link errors). Likewise `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_{init,update,final}` are already provided by the aead package; those P4 entries were satisfied without adding duplicates.\n- **`_sodium_blake2b_long` is mine** (per P4/quirks.h), implemented calling the extern `crypto_generichash_blake2b*` functions, matching the C `blake2b-long.c` two-branch logic byte-for-byte.\n- Preserved exact validation order, error codes (errno EFBIG/EINVAL/ENOMEM via `libc::__errno_location`), unsigned wraparound (`wrapping_*`) in `index_alpha`/fBlaMka/salsa, the argon2 encoded-string format, and `strchr`-on-NUL semantics in scrypt's `decode64_one`.\n- `argon2_context`/`argon2_instance_t`/`block_region`/`escrypt_region_t` are `#[repr(C)]` matching the C ABI (these structs cross the exported `_sodium_argon2_*`/`_sodium_escrypt_*` boundaries).\n\nNo files outside `src/pwhash/` were modified. Remaining compiler output is warnings only (dead assignments that mirror the C control flow, unused imports elsewhere in the crate).","usage":{"total_tokens":182301,"tool_uses":58,"duration_ms":1143864},"uuid":"9cb37102-bbd3-4511-a78f-af27ab4b8a5e","session_id":"8da51a24-6452-4245-bede-fa7b9c735887"}
