{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a01defe720067c59b","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QMRbe4kNfhKcFKrz5C57Qh","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-31072124/-tmp-harvest-translate-shxmUI-translated-rust/8da51a24-6452-4245-bede-fa7b9c735887/tasks/a01defe720067c59b.output","summary":"Build is clean (no errors) and all 169 P5 symbols are exported with zero missing.\n\n## Summary\n\nTranslated the P5 package (kdf/kem/kx/xof/ipcrypt/softaes) of libsodium 1.0.23 from C to Rust. All work is confined to `/tmp/harvest-translate-shxmUI/translated_rust/src/kdf_kem/`.\n\n**Files created:**\n- `src/kdf_kem/softaes.rs` — pure-software AES using the constant-time bitsliced (SRM-1R) reference path (non-FAVOR_PERFORMANCE, since not wasm). Exports all 9 `_sodium_softaes_*` symbols plus internal block load/store/xor helpers used by ipcrypt.\n- `src/kdf_kem/xof.rs` — shake128/256 + turboshake128/256. A shared state-machine driven by a macro, parameterized by RATE (168/136) and permutation (24-round for shake, 12-round for turboshake, called via extern to P1's keccak core). Exports all `_sodium_*_ref*` and `crypto_xof_*` symbols.\n- `src/kdf_kem/kdf.rs` — crypto_kdf dispatch, kdf_blake2b, and hkdf_sha256/sha512. Calls blake2b (P1) and HMAC (P3/aead) via extern; errno=EINVAL set via `__errno_location`.\n- `src/kdf_kem/kx.rs` — crypto_kx and `crypto_scalarmult_base` (which was not yet defined by any other package).\n- `src/kdf_kem/ipcrypt.rs` — crypto_ipcrypt + ipcrypt_soft, the `ipcrypt_soft_implementation` static (function-pointer struct, exported data symbol), and `_crypto_ipcrypt_pick_best_implementation`.\n- `src/kdf_kem/kem.rs` — crypto_kem dispatch + xwing.\n- `src/kdf_kem/mlkem.rs` — full ML-KEM-768 reference (poly/polyvec/ntt/indcpa/kem) with wrapping arithmetic matching C's int16/int32/uint32 truncation semantics for byte-identical output.\n\n`src/kdf_kem/mod.rs` declares the seven submodules.\n\n**Key findings / decisions:**\n- P5.txt lists a few symbols (`crypto_generichash`, `crypto_hash_sha3512`, `crypto_auth_hmacsha512_init/update/final`) attributed to my C files that are actually defined by other already-built packages (aead/P1). Redefining them would cause duplicate-symbol errors, so I call them via `extern \"C\"` instead. `crypto_scalarmult_base` was genuinely undefined, so I defined it in kx.rs per P5_files.txt.\n- softaes uses the bitsliced `#else` branch (FAVOR_PERFORMANCE is only set on wasm).\n- `GEN_MATRIX_NBLOCKS` evaluates to 3 for ML-KEM-768.\n\n**Verification:** `cargo build --release` finishes with no errors (only harmless cross-module extern-signature-mismatch warnings). The missing-P5-symbol check (`comm -13`) prints nothing — final missing count is **0**.","usage":{"total_tokens":205046,"tool_uses":65,"duration_ms":1043205},"uuid":"f1c25fa6-396a-4b02-b4bb-71db75212144","session_id":"8da51a24-6452-4245-bede-fa7b9c735887"}
