es (`crypto_core/softaes/softaes.c`) exporting all `_sodium_softaes_*` symbols (used by ipcrypt AND by the aead package via extern — you OWN and export these).\n\nC sources under `/tmp/harvest-translate-shxmUI/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/`. DO NOT modify c_src/. Translate ONLY reference/portable paths (no HAVE_* macros → shake/turboshake use keccak ref; mlkem768 uses ref; ipcrypt uses soft; softaes is the pure-software AES). Reproduce behavior EXACTLY (bugs, validation order, return values) for byte-identical output.\n\nWORK LOCATION: write Rust files ONLY inside `/tmp/harvest-translate-shxmUI/translated_rust/src/kdf_kem/`. Organize into submodules, declared in `src/kdf_kem/mod.rs`. Do NOT edit `src/lib.rs` or other package directories.\n\nCRITICAL — call primitives from other (already-done) packages via `extern \"C\"` (final linker names; signatures from headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`). You will need (do NOT reimplement):\n- keccak: `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_init`, `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_permute_24`, `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_permute_12`, `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_xor_bytes`, `_sodium_keccak1600_ref_extract_bytes`, `crypto_core_keccak1600_permute_24` (P1) — used by shake/turboshake.\n- hashes: `crypto_hash_sha256`, `crypto_hash_sha512`, `crypto_hash_sha3256`, `crypto_hash_sha3512` and their streaming forms (P1).\n- generichash/blake2b for kdf_blake2b: `crypto_generichash_blake2b_salt_personal` etc. (P1).\n- hmac for hkdf: `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_*`, `crypto_auth_hmacsha512_*` (P3).\n- scalarmult/x25519 for xwing/kx: `crypto_scalarmult_curve25519`, `crypto_scalarmult_curve25519_base`, `crypto_scalarmult`, `crypto_scalarmult_base` (P2).\n- foundation: `randombytes_buf`, `sodium_memzero`, `sodium_misuse`, `sodium_memcmp`.\nUndefined externs are fine in a cdylib. NOTE: you must EXPORT the `_sodium_softaes_*` symbols (they are in P5.txt); the aead package calls them via extern.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n- Each exported symbol: `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe exter